      "note_id": "borrowed_between_english_and_hindi",
      "kind": "helpful_transfer",
      "text": "English and Hindi are very distant cousins, so true look-alike words are rare and hard to spot. Most of these are Hindi words that English borrowed, some of them by way of Persian or other Indian languages. Then come a few English words that Hindi borrowed, which are fun to read in Devanagari, and a few old family words that really do share a root with English.",
